1
00:00:00,199 --> 00:00:03,360
Hi,  and  welcome  back  to  act.  Last

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:05,000
time,  we  looked  at  the  roles  you

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,640
have  and  the  communities  those

4
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:08,400
roles  connect  you  to.

5
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,960
Now  imagine  looking  at  one  of

6
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:12,400
those  communities  more  closely.  You

7
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,160
will  probably  notice  two  things  at

8
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:15,920
the  same  time.  Things  that  are

9
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:17,880
working  well  and  things  that  could

10
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:19,320
be  better.

11
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:21,400
Social  awareness  means  learning  to

12
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:23,599
notice  both.  If  you  only  see

13
00:00:23,599 --> 00:00:25,560
problems,  you  miss  the  strengths

14
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:27,800
already  available.  If  you  only  see

15
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,840
strengths,  you  may  ignore  people

16
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:31,480
who  are  struggling.

17
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:33,280
Understanding  a  community  means

18
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:36,079
holding  both  views  together.  Both

19
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:36,791
matter.

20
00:00:36,791 --> 00:00:38,711
One  way  people  contribute  to  a

21
00:00:38,711 --> 00:00:41,351
community  is  through  volunteering.

22
00:00:41,351 --> 00:00:43,031
Volunteering  is  work  a  person

23
00:00:43,031 --> 00:00:45,111
gives  to  society  without  expecting

24
00:00:45,111 --> 00:00:47,031
a  reward  in  return.

25
00:00:47,031 --> 00:00:48,550
That  does  not  mean  the  volunteer

26
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:50,590
learns  nothing  or  gains  nothing

27
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:51,911
personally.

28
00:00:51,911 --> 00:00:53,671
People  may  develop  skills,

29
00:00:53,671 --> 00:00:55,871
experience  or  stronger  connections

30
00:00:55,871 --> 00:00:57,271
through  service.

31
00:00:57,271 --> 00:00:59,671
The  difference  is  the  purpose.  The

32
00:00:59,671 --> 00:01:01,591
action  begins  with  contributing  to

33
00:01:01,591 --> 00:01:03,511
a  need,  not  with  demanding  a

34
00:01:03,511 --> 00:01:04,951
reward.

35
00:01:04,951 --> 00:01:06,830
Volunteering  is  one  way  a  person

36
00:01:06,830 --> 00:01:08,711
can  turn  awareness  of  a  community

37
00:01:08,711 --> 00:01:10,951
into  useful  action.  Even  when  the

38
00:01:10,951 --> 00:01:12,951
action  itself  is  small,

39
00:01:12,951 --> 00:01:15,166
that  makes  contribution  practical.

40
00:01:15,166 --> 00:01:17,886
Think  about  a  simple  example.  A

41
00:01:17,886 --> 00:01:20,445
fallen  tree  blocks  a  road  and  one

42
00:01:20,445 --> 00:01:22,605
child  starts  trying  to  move  it.

43
00:01:22,605 --> 00:01:24,286
The  child  cannot  solve  the  problem

44
00:01:24,286 --> 00:01:26,326
alone  at  first,  but  the  action

45
00:01:26,326 --> 00:01:28,885
gets  other  people  moving  too.

46
00:01:28,885 --> 00:01:30,845
The  useful  point  is  not  that  one

47
00:01:30,845 --> 00:01:33,006
person  must  do  everything.  It  is

48
00:01:33,006 --> 00:01:34,846
that  initiative  can  begin  when

49
00:01:34,846 --> 00:01:36,766
someone  notices  a  problem  and

50
00:01:36,766 --> 00:01:39,285
takes  a  reasonable  first  step.

51
00:01:39,285 --> 00:01:40,726
Sometimes  other  people  choose  to

52
00:01:40,726 --> 00:01:42,525
join  once  they  see  that  action  is

53
00:01:42,525 --> 00:01:44,046
possible.

54
00:01:44,046 --> 00:01:45,566
A  community  can  change When

55
00:01:45,566 --> 00:01:47,806
awareness  moves  from  someone  should

56
00:01:47,806 --> 00:01:50,686
do  something  to  what  useful  step

57
00:01:50,686 --> 00:01:52,326
can  begin  here.

58
00:01:52,326 --> 00:01:54,126
That  shift  is  what  initiative

59
00:01:54,126 --> 00:01:54,999
looks  like.

60
00:01:54,999 --> 00:01:57,239
contribution  can  benefit  both  the

61
00:01:57,239 --> 00:01:58,799
community  and  the  person

62
00:01:58,799 --> 00:02:00,119
contributing.

63
00:02:00,119 --> 00:02:01,798
A  community  may  gain  a  cleaner

64
00:02:01,798 --> 00:02:04,239
space,  better  support,  useful

65
00:02:04,239 --> 00:02:06,678
knowledge  or  help  with  a  problem.

66
00:02:06,678 --> 00:02:08,319
At  the  same  time,  the  person

67
00:02:08,319 --> 00:02:10,638
involved  may  practice  communication,

68
00:02:10,638 --> 00:02:12,959
organization,  problem  solving  or

69
00:02:12,959 --> 00:02:14,438
another  skill.

70
00:02:14,438 --> 00:02:16,278
Imagine  people  helping  improve

71
00:02:16,278 --> 00:02:17,919
buildings  in  their  village  while

72
00:02:17,919 --> 00:02:19,438
learning  practical  construction

73
00:02:19,438 --> 00:02:21,438
skills  through  the  process.

74
00:02:21,438 --> 00:02:22,999
The  point  is  not  to  promise  a

75
00:02:22,999 --> 00:02:25,518
job  or  a  reward.  It  is  to  show

76
00:02:25,518 --> 00:02:28,039
that  serving  a  real  need  can  also

77
00:02:28,039 --> 00:02:29,519
become  a  place  where  useful

78
00:02:29,519 --> 00:02:31,119
abilities  are  practiced  and

79
00:02:31,119 --> 00:02:32,082
strengthened.

80
00:02:32,082 --> 00:02:33,882
A  useful  way  to  understand  a

81
00:02:33,882 --> 00:02:36,602
community  is  to  map  what  you  see.

82
00:02:36,602 --> 00:02:38,762
Use  green  spots  for  strengths  and

83
00:02:38,762 --> 00:02:40,842
opportunities,  red  spots  for

84
00:02:40,842 --> 00:02:42,922
problems  or  negative  conditions,

85
00:02:42,922 --> 00:02:44,721
and  black  points  for  possible

86
00:02:44,721 --> 00:02:46,801
reasons  behind  a  problem.

87
00:02:46,801 --> 00:02:48,482
A  green  spot  might  be  supportive

88
00:02:48,482 --> 00:02:50,922
people,  useful  resources,  local

89
00:02:50,922 --> 00:02:53,322
knowledge,  or  a  good  facility.

90
00:02:53,322 --> 00:02:55,361
A  red  spot  might  be  littering,

91
00:02:55,361 --> 00:02:57,802
unemployment,  smoking,  unsafe

92
00:02:57,802 --> 00:02:59,802
spaces,  or  another  issue  affecting

93
00:02:59,802 --> 00:03:00,922
people.

94
00:03:00,922 --> 00:03:02,761
A  black  point  as  asks  a  different

95
00:03:02,761 --> 00:03:05,082
question.  What  may  be  contributing

96
00:03:05,082 --> 00:03:06,562
to  that  problem?

97
00:03:06,562 --> 00:03:08,122
The  map  helps  you  separate  what

98
00:03:08,122 --> 00:03:10,362
is  good,  what  is  difficult,  and

99
00:03:10,362 --> 00:03:11,832
what  may  be  behind  it.

100
00:03:11,832 --> 00:03:13,752
Try  this  as  an  individual

101
00:03:13,752 --> 00:03:16,191
reflection.  Choose  one  community

102
00:03:16,191 --> 00:03:18,591
you  know  well,  your  neighborhood,

103
00:03:18,591 --> 00:03:21,632
school,  university,  workplace,  or

104
00:03:21,632 --> 00:03:23,952
another  place  you  regularly  see.

105
00:03:23,952 --> 00:03:26,471
Picture  it  like  a  simple  map.

106
00:03:26,471 --> 00:03:28,672
First,  mark  two  or  three  green

107
00:03:28,672 --> 00:03:31,512
spots,  strengths,  resources,  or

108
00:03:31,512 --> 00:03:32,832
opportunities.

109
00:03:32,832 --> 00:03:34,871
Then,  mark  two  or  three  red

110
00:03:34,871 --> 00:03:37,512
spots,  problems  or  difficulties  you

111
00:03:37,512 --> 00:03:39,511
have  genuinely  noticed.

112
00:03:39,511 --> 00:03:41,871
For  one  red  spot,  write  one

113
00:03:41,871 --> 00:03:43,911
possible  reason  beside  it.

114
00:03:43,911 --> 00:03:45,352
You're  not  trying  to  prove  the

115
00:03:45,352 --> 00:03:47,112
cause  yet.  The  goal  is  to

116
00:03:47,112 --> 00:03:49,152
separate  what  you  observe  from

117
00:03:49,152 --> 00:03:51,432
what  you  think  may  be  causing  it.

118
00:03:51,432 --> 00:03:52,957
That  distinction  matters.

119
00:03:52,957 --> 00:03:55,677
Now,  add  one  more  layer.

120
00:03:55,677 --> 00:03:57,357
Where  could  your  own  abilities

121
00:03:57,357 --> 00:03:58,316
fit?

122
00:03:58,316 --> 00:03:59,997
Maybe  you  are  good  at  explaining

123
00:03:59,997 --> 00:04:02,837
ideas,  organizing  information,

124
00:04:02,837 --> 00:04:05,676
listening,  designing,  writing,

125
00:04:05,676 --> 00:04:08,476
technology,  sports,  or  practical

126
00:04:08,476 --> 00:04:09,717
work.

127
00:04:09,717 --> 00:04:11,597
You  do  not  need  to  solve  every

128
00:04:11,597 --> 00:04:13,316
red  spot  on  the  map.

129
00:04:13,316 --> 00:04:15,437
Contribution  starts  by  noticing

130
00:04:15,437 --> 00:04:17,637
where  a  real  need  and  a  useful

131
00:04:17,637 --> 00:04:19,877
ability  might  connect.

132
00:04:19,877 --> 00:04:21,357
Sometimes  that  connection  becomes

133
00:04:21,357 --> 00:04:23,357
volunteering.  Sometimes times  it

134
00:04:23,357 --> 00:04:25,676
becomes  an  initiative  later.

135
00:04:25,676 --> 00:04:27,836
For  now,  the  important  skill  is

136
00:04:27,836 --> 00:04:29,516
seeing  your  community  as  a  place

137
00:04:29,516 --> 00:04:32,356
with  both  needs  and  resources,  not

138
00:04:32,356 --> 00:04:33,797
only  as  a  place  where  you  happen

139
00:04:33,797 --> 00:04:34,623
to  live.

